= Related Work

Specifically related to the realistic aspect of the work several studies have been conducted: between them, a 2022 study, "The use of virtual reality in environment experiences and the importance of realism" tested, in the second study, how realism can impact people that are recovering from a stressful situation reacted to several level of realism in virtual reality environment@study.

The paper describes how presence obtained higher scores on high realism environments and immersion was partially compromised by the virtual space size@study.

However, the study put an attention on scenes with not an higher level of interaction, while our game, while providing a less realistic scene, involves more interaction and involvement in the virtual world, therefore allowing to understand how an higher level of interaction could compromise the lower level of realism, allowing an higher sense of presence and immersion.

Other papers that analyzed how to intensify horror experiences exists, like the 2023 "Decoding Fear: Exploring User Experiences in Virtual Reality Horror Games"@study2, also exists.